# -- end of source
# `for (const value of unmatched(..)) return value;`: the loop over the generator returns in its first turn, so the step stands in the block of the call and of the open. A generator of more than one yield is
# not walked in place where the region of the iteration itself holds an iteration that is walked in place; the rule read the whole block and so counted the open of this very generator against it: the
# generator was made, stepped by a stub and closed: 316 instructions a call more. What stands in front of the step is no part of the region.
# f1 = unmatched, f2 = first
# RUN: walk f2:Body mechanisms=all
# CHECK-LABEL: code f2:Body
# CHECK-NOT: coroutine(f1)
# CHECK-NOT: = StepGenerator
# RUN(SHELL): run-in-shell globalThis.sink = print;
# SHELL: d4 d8 b10 c13 b15 undefined15
